{"tool_name":"sctam-seq","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"sctam-seq","home":"https://github.com/veltenlab/scTAM-seq-scripts","license":"MIT","summary":"scTAM-seq enables targeted high-confidence analysis of DNA methylation in single cells.","addition_date":"2022-12-12T20:45:19.897558Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:18:01.279116Z","tool_type":["Script"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:sctam-seq","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"renee.beekman@crg.eu","name":"Ren\u00e9e Beekman","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7081-7874","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"lars.velten@crg.eu","name":"Lars Velten","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Agostina Bianchi"},{"name":"Michael Scherer"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"DNA barcoding","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3200"},{"term":"DNA profiling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3894"},{"term":"Essential dynamics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3891"},{"term":"Methylation analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3204"}]}],"name":"scTAM-seq","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s13059-022-02796-7","metadata":{"abstract":"Single-cell DNA methylation profiling currently suffers from excessive noise and/or limited cellular throughput. We developed scTAM-seq, a targeted bisulfite-free method for profiling up to 650 CpGs in up to 10,000 cells per experiment, with a dropout rate as low as 7%. We demonstrate that scTAM-seq can resolve DNA methylation dynamics across B-cell differentiation in blood and bone marrow, identifying intermediate differentiation states that were previously masked. scTAM-seq additionally queries surface-protein expression, thus enabling integration of single-cell DNA methylation information with cell atlas data. In summary, scTAM-seq is a high-throughput, high-confidence method for analyzing DN